- **apps (rdme, examples, accesskit_xplat; `bump` left the workspace with upstream's `23b9b26a9` "Delete the bump crate", merged at 2026-10-17-upstream-sync-engine-debts):** no tests — observed absent · searched: `#\[(tokio::)?test\]` over the 86 files of slice s04 (hits only in the five browser files above); `examples/seven_guis` holds eight integration-test targets (seven until 2026-10-19-session-recording added `tests/recording.rs`), one shared module that is no target, `tests/common/mod.rs` (the state directory, the leftover clear, the kill-and-reap `Host` guard and, since 2026-10-10-driver-cli, the stream drain, one bounded run of the binary as a client — `Ran`, `run`, `client` — the readers of an answer's one line, `keys`, `number` and `cause`, and the `Started` guard that stops a started session; since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface `string_at`, the outer-layer reader of a JSON string, and `Speaker` with `Spoke` — a child spoken to over piped stdin, its stdout read line by line on a thread under the 30 s `REPLY_BOUND`, every reply asserted free of an ESC byte, the child killed and reaped in its `Drop`; since 2026-10-19-test-splits the log checks' fragment, stated once — `Needles` and `stand_needles` (the CRUD stand's id and name needles, asserted non-empty and no part of the sentinel), `stamped_lines` (every stderr line stamped `service.name=seven_guis`), `found`, `occurrences` and the unix-only `recorded_needles` — called by `host_log` and `mcp_log` alone (examples/seven_guis/tests/common/mod.rs:371-514); read through `mod common;` by all eight) and a script directory that is no target, `tests/flows/`: since 2026-10-07-driver-session `tests/host_binary.rs` (2 tests)
 — the `escher-session` binary in its host role, `serve <task> --session <dir> [--record <dir>]`, serves a counter session, answers under the binary's own pid, stops, exits 0 with nothing on stdout, its stderr stamped `service.name=seven_guis`, and leaves no state directory, and a host that cannot serve ends as a session error, exit 3; nine argv rows that are no command each end as a usage error, exit 2, their usage line holding nothing the caller typed, with nothing booted and no state created — run as `cargo test -p seven_guis --locked --test host_binary`; and since 2026-10-07-sink-target-allowlist `tests/host_log.rs` (3 tests, unix only; 1 until 2026-10-19-session-recording added a recording host that logs nothing of its check at `trace`, and the third reading the clients of a recording session — `start crud --record` through `stop`, a part read and a `lint` among them — 0 needles of each class over their own stderr at `trace`, examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:42-132) — the `escher-session` binary on `crud` at `RUST_LOG=trace` exits 0 with nothing on stdout and no state directory, every stderr line stamped `service.name=seven_guis`, and no stable id and no accessible name on stderr, its needles read from the stand itself, and since 2026-10-10-driver-cli while a hosted `snapshot`, `click` and `type` run on it: three `command` span lines for the three calls, and 0 occurrences of the typed sentinel beside 0 ids and 0 names — run as `cargo test -p seven_guis --locked --test host_log` and, for the host the workspace build makes, as `cargo test --workspace --locked --test host_log`; since 2026-10-10-driver-cli `tests/cli_commands.rs` (13 tests, unix only: every driver command run as a process of the binary — §6 → Drivers per surface; since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot a `screenshot` answering one line whose `png`, decoded by a hand base64 reader and its PNG header, equals the PNG `Session::run` returns in process;
 since 2026-10-12-self-description `help` answering the tool's description and reaching no session, and a state directory of 94 bytes holding a session where one of 95 is refused `state-dir-too-long` with its bound, and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, on every target but Linux one of 90 bytes holding a session where one of 91 ends `state-dir-too-long`, status 3, its message holding no path — the two through one shared helper that asserts the message holds not the given directory, so the 94 case asserts it too; the file counts 11 on Linux and 11 on macOS, the 90 case measured on the macOS matrix leg, CI#38642493451, job 116123587286 — examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:719-723; since 2026-10-14-quality-gates a run with its stdout closed before it starts keeps its ending's status — `help` 0, `snapshot` with no session 3 with exactly `NoSession`'s message — printing no panic and creating no state directory, examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:649-711), `tests/cli_flow.rs` (2, unix only: the two shell flows of `tests/flows/` under plain `sh`) and `tests/host_timer.rs` (1, unix only: the timer host moved by a hosted `advance`) — run as `cargo test -p seven_guis --locked --test {name}`; since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface `tests/mcp_server.rs` (6 tests: the binary's `mcp` role completes the Counter flow by tool calls alone — `initialize`, `tools/list` offering the verbs in order, twelve, `start`, `snapshot`, `click` — answers a `lint` tool call with its line of findings, and answers a `server/discover`, a non-JSON line, a 65,537-byte line, an unknown tool, a refused and a malformed call each without running anything, the next snapshot equal and no reply holding the refused id, the tool name or the filler; and, unix only, a fresh Counter's `snapshot` reads the same through MCP and through the command line;
 since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot a `screenshot` tool call answered with an image block then a text block (examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_server.rs:308-338); since 2026-10-12-self-description the newest revision `2025-11-25` spoken — `2026-07-28` answered with it — and `help` answered before any `start`, and, unix only, `help` reading the same bytes through MCP and through the command line) and `tests/mcp_log.rs` (2 tests — 1 until 2026-10-19-session-recording added a recording `mcp` role that logs nothing of its checks at `trace`, unix-gated, reading the shared `common::recorded_needles` (its own until 2026-10-19-test-splits): the role on `crud` at `RUST_LOG=trace` writes 0 typed-sentinel occurrences, 0 id needles and 0 name needles on stderr, one `tool_call` line per call with only its stated field names, and protocol lines only on stdout; since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot it and `host_log` also drive shots and read 0 occurrences of a shot's first 64 base64 characters on stderr, under both builds — examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:398-411; examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_log.rs:141-154) — not unix-gated but the CLI comparisons, two since 2026-10-12-self-description (examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_server.rs:360-380; examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_server.rs:382-423), so the windows job runs them, run as `cargo test -p seven_guis --locked --test mcp_server --test mcp_log` and, for the workspace build, `cargo test --workspace --locked --test mcp_server --test mcp_log`; since 2026-10-19-session-recording `tests/recording.rs` (4 tests, unix only, and 1 off-unix; 3 until 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay) — the command line and the `mcp` role keep the same check byte for byte, the state directory gone after `stop`; a recording directory open to its group refused before anything runs; the `mcp` role's listing and `help` the same with and without `--record`;
 since 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay the committed checks what the binary records, `record_checks.sh` run through the binary and both files compared byte for byte with the committed copies (examples/seven_guis/tests/recording.rs:205-262); off unix, `--record` refused `Unsupported` — run as `cargo test -p seven_guis --locked --test recording` and in the stand-repeat leg; and since 2026-10-07-act-by-id the library's first unit test, `stand::tests::the_timer_step_carries_milliseconds_onto_whole_ticks` — six cumulative rows of milliseconds onto Timer ticks and two carry rows, the remainder below one tick carried across calls — and `stand::tests::the_timer_step_takes_the_largest_advance` (examples/seven_guis/src/stand.rs:331-343), run as `cargo test -p seven_guis --locked --lib stand::`, and since 2026-10-16-fast-failing-mutants its second, `tasks::timer::tests::a_delivered_tick_is_taken_once_and_an_empty_wait_parks`, in a `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` after the Timer's `CSS` constant, polling the private `TimerTicks::next()` under `Waker::noop()` over a three-row table, the row count asserted, `TimerTicks::next` keeping its one caller, `Timer` (examples/seven_guis/src/tasks/timer.rs:197-226) — `cargo test -p seven_guis --locked --lib` reads 3 passed, as measured at escher-0.2.0/chunks/2026-10-18-one-virtual-clock/report.md; since 2026-10-10-driver-cli `host_timer` boots `escher-session` on `timer`, the one task whose session carries a time step, and moves it by a hosted `advance` with no sleep — 250 ms asked reads `advanced_ms` 250 with the elapsed text two ticks on, every ask reporting exactly the `ms` asked (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18) — and `cli_commands` starts, reads and stops all four tasks; until then that branch of the host was booted by hand only (escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-act-by-id/evidence/timer-host-boot.md);
 the other examples — the root example `multi_doc`, built by `cargo build --workspace` within `fast`'s clippy, among them — and the apps named still hold no tests (examples/seven_guis/tests/host_binary.rs:19-159; examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:30-492; examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:134-617; examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:618-792; examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_flow.rs:31-88; examples/seven_guis/tests/host_timer.rs:22-126; examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_server.rs:100-259; examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_server.rs:261-381; examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_server.rs:382-423; examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_log.rs:51-266; examples/seven_guis/tests/common/mod.rs:1-514; examples/seven_guis/src/stand.rs:246-344; the two MCP targets as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-mcp-surface/report.md, the four new tests at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-12-self-description/report.md, the screenshot's two and the image-byte readings at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-12-headless-screenshot/report.md)

- **escher-driver:** 100 unit tests in sixteen files, 64 inline and 36 in four `#[path]` test files (72 inline and 20 in two from 2026-10-16-file-splits until 2026-10-19-test-splits), beside three off-unix tests the windows job alone runs, recording's one in a fifth `#[path]` file, `recording_off_unix_tests.rs`, since 2026-10-19-test-splits (94 in sixteen, 60 inline and 34 in four `#[path]` files, until 2026-10-20-load-wait, 92 in fifteen until 2026-10-19-visual-lint, 87 in fourteen until 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay, 74 in thirteen until 2026-10-19-session-recording, 73 until 2026-10-16-fast-failing-mutants, 72 until 2026-10-14-quality-gates, 66 in twelve until 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot, 59 in eleven until 2026-10-12-self-description, 50 in ten until 2026-10-10-mcp-surface, 29 in seven until 2026-10-10-driver-cli) — error.rs 5 (every `SessionError` message — all fifteen variants (thirteen until 2026-10-19-session-recording), `NotSettled` in each of its three classes and `AnswerTooLarge` included — is non-empty and holds no path, an exit code is not in the message, the `Io` message adds the kind's name; since 2026-10-12-self-description the errors — fifteen since 2026-10-19-session-recording added `RecordDirNotPrivate` and `RecordingFailed` — each state a kind, a meaning and a remedy, and the state directory's message states its bound), session.rs 10 (6 until 2026-10-20-load-wait, which added the load wait's four over a scripted settle — a load answered inside the bound ends the wait settled, one never answered ends it at the bound, work other than a load returns at once, a quiet settle returns after one settle; 4 until 2026-10-19-session-recording, which added that a recording directory open to others is refused with nothing written and that a recording that ends reads failed once; a label of the closed set is valid;
 a label outside it is refused before the boot runs; the session's record holds the ids it read and, past its bound, forgets the one read longest ago; and the record holds no id longer than a call can name), wire.rs 12 (each request and each reply of the `v3` grammar — `v2` until 2026-10-19-session-recording — round-trips: `hello`, `stop` and `call`, the lifecycle replies and `accepted` · `refused` · `oversize` · `recording-failed` — a known word with another version is refused by version, anything else and bytes that are not text are refused as malformed, 51 malformed rows, a reply outside the protocol does not parse, a line is read up to its terminator and no further, an over-long line and an unterminated one are named; a byte that is not plain is written as its escape, a decoded call is the call that was encoded, the widest call the schema admits fits the 16,384-byte request bound, and an answer at its 1,048,576-byte bound is carried while one byte over is not), refusal.rs 3 (the causes are named in order — eight (`the_eight_causes_are_named_in_order`, ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18), `fonts-unavailable` last; each cause states its meaning and its remedy — against a stated table, non-empty, remedies pairwise distinct, no `/` in any text; a refusal reads as its cause's name, then its remedy), schema_tests.rs 7 (`schema::tests`, in schema.rs until 2026-10-16-file-splits; 6 until 2026-10-20-load-wait, which added that the `settled` help states `LOAD_WAIT` in whole seconds, that the five acting verbs carry that field and that the wait ends before an answer read; the verbs are named in order, each at its level — eight instance-level (`screenshot` the seventh, after `scroll`, and `lint` the eighth, after `screenshot`), then `start` · `status` · `stop`, then, since 2026-10-12-self-description, `help` at the tool level, twelve;
 every verb states its help, its arguments and a result; a verb is found by its exact name only; each verb has its stated argument and result shapes, and the kinds with their bound texts, the twelve key names, the node fields and the busy classes read as stated; since that chunk the thirteen node keys are named in order, each with its help, and the four exit statuses are stated in status order), command.rs 7 (an admitted call becomes its command; an unknown verb is refused as `unknown-verb`; a verb is checked at its own level only — `validate` refuses a session-level verb and `validate_session` an instance-level one; a malformed session call and a malformed call are each refused with the rule they broke; a call that breaks two rules gets the first in the order; every verb of the table is reached and names its own spec), execute.rs 3 (each of the schema's twelve keys stands for one keyboard key — 12 rows, pairwise distinct; the command span has its eight fields — `verb` · `cause` · `settled` · `busy` · `passes` · `added` · `removed` · `changed` — and none is the name of one of the table's eight arguments; each busy class reads as its schema word) and, since 2026-10-10-driver-cli, json.rs 7 (a string is written with its escapes; a number as the shortest decimal and `null` when not finite; a node with the schema fields it has, a masked value as the mask; a lint's outcome as `{"findings":[…]}`, each finding keyed `id` · `defect` · `bounds` then its reason's keys, every reason pinned and a ratio that is not finite written `null`; each outcome with its verb's fields in order; each refusal from its cause's fixed strings; each session error with its kind and its message and, since 2026-10-12-self-description, its remedy; each session answer with its verb's fields in order;
 since that chunk a changed node with `differs` after `bounds`), cli_tests.rs 5 (`cli::tests`, in `cli.rs` until 2026-10-19-test-splits — a line is read by its rules in order — 64 rows since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface, the `mcp` role's three among them, 61 until then; an argument that is not text is a usage error; each ending writes its streams and returns its status; the usage line is built from the table and the apps; a line that is no command or is refused runs nothing) client.rs 3 (a call's reply reads as its answer or as a session error; a call the schema refuses is answered without a session; since 2026-10-14-quality-gates, in a unix-only `client::imp::tests`, the answer's per-read bound pinned equal to `wire::ANSWER_BOUND`, 30 s, and a read past a shortened bound on a listener that never answers ending as `SessionError::Timeout`) and, since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface, mcp_tests.rs 15 (12 until 2026-10-19-session-recording, which added that each session a recording boot starts is kept as one check and that a call that ends the recording is answered as its session error; `mcp::tests`, in mcp.rs until 2026-10-16-file-splits; 11 until 2026-10-16-fast-failing-mutants, 10 until 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot; each line is read by its rules; a line is read whole across reads and an unended last line is one; since 2026-10-16-fast-failing-mutants `framing::read_request` takes each line with its terminator over a slice and over a one-byte `BufReader`, each reader making at most its line count plus one reads, the count asserted (packages/escher-driver/src/mcp_tests.rs:167-196); an id is echoed only in its two forms; each method gets its reply; each argument value becomes its kind or refuses the call; the listing is the twelve verbs of the table, `snapshot`'s tool taking an optional integer `part` and naming its two counts; the session verbs are answered by the server;
 since 2026-10-12-self-description `help` is answered by the server with or without a session; since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot a result that holds an image is bounded by its whole written form, and a shot is written as its image block then its text block, a refused one as one text block (packages/escher-driver/src/mcp_tests.rs:754-785); a session idle for its expiry is dropped when a request arrives; a result over the answer bound is replaced by the session error — the sessions they hold booted from an empty app) and, since 2026-10-12-self-description, describe.rs 2 (the document holds `help`'s seven fields in order; every text in it is its tables'; its count row reads `[12, 13, 12, 3, 8, 4, 15]`), since 2026-10-19-session-recording recording_tests.rs 9 (`recording::tests`, in `recording.rs` until 2026-10-19-test-splits — the digest is FNV-1a 64 of the written answer; a recording reads back as the calls it kept; a masked `type` keeps the stand-in and nothing of the text; a call no record can spell is not kept; the check and its directory are owner-only and no file is replaced; a recording that would pass its bound or cannot write ends and removes its check, never a temporary it did not create; each record keeps its answer after the digest, a shot's without `png`; a check in the grammar is read, 8 rows (6 until 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay added an object `answer`, a refusal's `answer` and keys out of order); one outside it is refused `malformed`, 40 rows (35 until then added `answer` missing, a string, a number, an array, `null` and an unknown key beside it); a check at its bounds is read and one past them refused), since 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay replay.rs 5 (a check replayed on a fresh session holds; an acceptance that flips is a change naming the keys that differ; a changed answer names its keys and stops the replay;
 a shot holds at its size whatever its pixels; a check of another app runs nothing — packages/escher-driver/src/replay.rs:141-318) and, since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot, image.rs 5 (the hand base64 reads the RFC 4648 test vectors and writes every sextet of the alphabet; a PNG decodes to the pixels it was given and holds no time or text chunk; pixels that do not fill the size write nothing — packages/escher-driver/src/image.rs:39-107) and, since 2026-10-19-visual-lint, lint.rs 2 (`Defect::ALL` names the six defects in order; findings follow document order, then the defect order — packages/escher-driver/src/lint.rs:526-604); host.rs holds no unit test — the socket, the spawn, each lifecycle edge, a hosted call and the idle expiry are covered by `stand_session_lifecycle` and seven_guis' `host_binary` and `cli_commands`; the executor's verbs and its refusals are covered by the fifteen `stand_act_*` integration files (`stand_act_screenshot` the thirteenth, `stand_act_transformed` the fourteenth, `stand_act_select` the fifteenth), and, since 2026-10-19-visual-lint, `Session::lint`'s readings over a held instance by `stand_lint`, not by a unit test — the crate depends on nothing that names a virtual DOM, so a unit test cannot build a held instance, and its JSON writer's node rows are tested over plain parts for the same reason; its doc-test line reads 0 (packages/escher-driver/src/error.rs:226-352; packages/escher-driver/src/session.rs:246-438; packages/escher-driver/src/wire.rs:305-738; packages/escher-driver/src/refusal.rs:203-336; packages/escher-driver/src/schema_tests.rs:1-404; packages/escher-driver/src/command.rs:378-905; packages/escher-driver/src/execute.rs:583-646; packages/escher-driver/src/json.rs:435-936; packages/escher-driver/src/cli_tests.rs:1-580; packages/escher-driver/src/client.rs:263-308; packages/escher-driver/src/client.rs:342-426;
 packages/escher-driver/src/mcp_tests.rs:1-786; packages/escher-driver/src/describe.rs:97-234) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-session/report.md, the count of 74 and mcp_tests.rs's twelfth at escher-0.2.0/chunks/2026-10-16-fast-failing-mutants/report.md, the count of 73 and client.rs's third at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-14-quality-gates/report.md, the count of 72, image.rs's five and mcp.rs's eleventh at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-12-headless-screenshot/report.md, the count of 66 and describe.rs's two at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-12-self-description/report.md, the count of 59 and mcp.rs's nine at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-mcp-surface/report.md, the count of 50, the three new test modules and the `v2` wire's rows at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-driver-cli/report.md, the three schema files and the count of 25 at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-command-and-refusal-schema/report.md, execute.rs and the count of 26 at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-act-by-id/report.md, session.rs's third test, the sixth verb's rows and the count of 27 at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-refusal-detection/report.md, execute.rs's two span tests and the count of 29 at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-command-spans/report.md
